<title>FRANCE: Matif commodities futures volume down in May.</title>
<headline>Matif commodities futures volume down in May.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of commodities futures and options traded on the French MATIF exchange in May fell 56.9 percent from the previous month and was down 33.9 percent compared with May 1996, operator Matif SA said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for commodity contracts were as follows.</p>
<p>			 Volume    Change	Change   Open positions</p>
<p>				     on month    on year   at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	10,735   -56.9 pct   -33.9 pct   10,750</p>
<p>  Total futures     10,735   -56.9 pct   -32.7 pct   10,750</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>    White sugar ($)  5,620   -64.6 pct   -33.8 pct    6,384</p>
<p>    Potatoes	     255   -68.8 pct   -69.8 pct	  0</p>
<p>    Rapeseed	   4,311   -21.6 pct   -34.9 pct    3,332</p>
<p>    Wheat		  549   -79.8 pct     N/A	  1,034</p>
<p>  Sugar options	    0					  0</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
